{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Python 3 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Python 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n<your_rewritten_code_2>\nimport sys\n\ndef main():\n    MOD = 1000000007\n    T = 1\n    \n    for _ in range(T):\n        P, K = map(int, input().split())\n        \n        if K == 0:\n            print(pow(P, P - 1, MOD))\n            continue\n        \n        # Precompute the permutation induced by multiplication by K mod P\n        perm = [K * i % P for i in range(P)]\n        \n        # Find cycle decomposition\n        visited = [False] * P\n        cycles = []\n        \n        for i in range(P):\n            if visited[i]:\n                continue\n            cycle = []\n            j = i\n            while not visited[j]:\n                visited[j] = True\n                cycle.append(j)\n                j = perm[j]\n            cycles.append(cycle)\n        \n        # Count cycles by length\n        from collections import Counter\n        length_counts = Counter(len(c) for c in cycles)\n        \n        ans = 1\n        for length, count in length_counts.items():\n            if length == 1:\n                effective = length * count\n            else:\n                effective = length * count + 1\n            ans = (ans * pow(effective, count, MOD)) % MOD\n        \n        print(ans)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</your_rewritten_code_2>\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static final long MOD = 1000000007;\n    \n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        String[] line = br.readLine().split(\" \");\n        int P = Integer.parseInt(line[0]);\n        int K = Integer.parseInt(line[1]);\n        \n        if (K == 0) {\n            System.out.println(powerMod(P, P - 1, MOD));\n            return;\n        }\n        \n        // Precompute the permutation induced by multiplication by K mod P\n        int[] perm = new int[P];\n        for (int i = 0; i < P; i++) {\n            perm[i] = (K * i) % P;\n        }\n        \n        // Find cycle decomposition\n        boolean[] visited = new boolean[P];\n        List<List<Integer>> cycles = new ArrayList<>();\n        \n        for (int i = 0; i < P; i++) {\n            if (visited[i]) {\n                continue;\n            }\n            List<Integer> cycle = new ArrayList<>();\n            int j = i;\n            while (!visited[j]) {\n                visited[j] = true;\n                cycle.add(j);\n                j = perm[j];\n            }\n            cycles.add(cycle);\n        }\n        \n        // Count cycles by length\n        Map<Integer, Integer> lengthCounts = new HashMap<>();\n        for (List<Integer> cycle : cycles) {\n            int len = cycle.size();\n            lengthCounts.put(len, lengthCounts.getOrDefault(len, 0) + 1);\n        }\n        \n        long ans = 1;\n        for (Map.Entry<Integer, Integer> entry : lengthCounts.entrySet()) {\n            int length = entry.getKey();\n            int count = entry.getValue();\n            long effective;\n            if (length == 1) {\n                effective = (long) length * count;\n            } else {\n                effective = (long) length * count + 1;\n            }\n            ans = (ans * powerMod(effective, count, MOD)) % MOD;\n        }\n        \n        System.out.println(ans);\n    }\n    \n    static long powerMod(long base, long exp, long mod) {\n        long result = 1;\n        base = base % mod;\n        while (exp > 0) {\n            if ((exp & 1) == 1) {\n                result = (result * base) % mod;\n            }\n            base = (base * base) % mod;\n            exp >>= 1;\n        }\n        return result;\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00016211149340961128, -2.50339189733495e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.00047267231275327504, -1.3351351299206726e-05, -0.011143825948238373, -0.16030971705913544, -0.0004146431456319988, -2.288792165927589e-05, -0.011201825924217701, -0.000339569611242041, -0.0002687808300834149, -1.5497195136049413e-06, -0.00011955977242905647, -0.006719138007611036, -0.0009120118920691311, -0.1136663556098938, -0.0010715939570218325, -0.0007364421617239714, -3.814689989667386e-06, 0.0, -3.576278118089249e-07, 0.0, -1.4305104514278355e-06, 0.0, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.145764938177308e-06, -0.06460584700107574, -2.622600959512056e-06, -5.960462772236497e-07, -0.12701772153377533, -2.0265558760002023e-06, -0.07889349013566971, -3.3378546504536644e-06, -7.629365427419543e-06, -2.0265558760002023e-06, -1.9073304429184645e-05, -8.344646857949556e-07, -0.009800885803997517, -0.005949288606643677, -5.960462772236497e-07, -3.3378546504536644e-06, -8.070142939686775e-05, -0.0003182381624355912, -8.344646857949556e-07, -4.768370445162873e-07, -6.794906312279636e-06, -3.93389882447